IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sk-sis`

-- The Saskatchewan Assistance Act and The Saskatchewan Income Support Regulations -- the questions of the individual who
-- applies for, or receives, Saskatchewan Income Support for their household. Every question calls the rules in sk-sis.l4;
-- nothing is restated here. Plain inputs, one per fact the person can state. Amounts are monthly, in Canadian dollars.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: the Act and Regulations are quoted from the King's Printer consolidations, (c) 2026, Government of
-- Saskatchewan; not an official version. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Can I apply`

@export Can I apply for Saskatchewan Income Support for my household under SIS Regulations s 2-1(3)?
GIVEN `I am ordinarily present in Saskatchewan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are ordinarily present (living) in Saskatchewan
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
      `my status in Canada` IS A `Status in Canada` @desc Your status in Canada: Canadian citizen, permanent resident, Convention refugee, holder of a temporary resident permit under IRPA s 24, refugee claimant or protection applicant awaiting a decision, subject to a removal order that cannot be executed, or another status such as a visitor, student or worker
      `the ministry waived the presence or residency requirement for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the ministry has waived the presence or residency requirement for you for compassionate, compelling or medical reasons (s 2-10(1)(d)); no if you have not been told so
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I apply` IF
    `may apply under s 2-1(3)` `I am ordinarily present in Saskatchewan` `my age` `my status in Canada` `the ministry waived the presence or residency requirement for me`

§ `Who in my household is left out`

@export Is a member of my household one for whom no Saskatchewan Income Support is paid, under SIS Regulations s 2-5?
GIVEN `days detained in a provincial jail or youth custody` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days the person has been detained in a provincial correctional facility or youth custody facility; 0 if none
      `is a federal inmate or a prisoner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person is an inmate in a federal penitentiary or a prisoner under the Prisons and Reformatories Act
      `lives on a reserve` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person is ordinarily resident on a reserve under the Indian Act
      `continuous days away from Saskatchewan` IS A NUMBER @desc How many continuous days the person has been absent from Saskatchewan; 0 if none
      `the ministry accepted the absence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the ministry is satisfied the absence is for compassionate, compelling or medical reasons
      `is an adult post-secondary student outside an approved program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person is an adult enrolled in a post-secondary program that is not an approved education and training program (s 4.1-3)
      `is serving a period of ineligibility under other assistance regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person has been found ineligible under the Saskatchewan Assistance Regulations, 2014 s 18 or the SAID Regulations s 20 and the period has not ended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this member left out` IF
    `no benefit is paid for the member under s 2-5` (`Household member's circumstances` WITH
        `days detained in a provincial correctional or youth custody facility` IS `days detained in a provincial jail or youth custody`
        `is a federal inmate or a prisoner` IS `is a federal inmate or a prisoner`
        `ordinarily resident on a reserve` IS `lives on a reserve`
        `continuous days absent from Saskatchewan` IS `continuous days away from Saskatchewan`
        `the minister accepts the absence as compassionate, compelling or medical` IS `the ministry accepted the absence`
        `adult student in a post-secondary program that is not an approved program` IS `is an adult post-secondary student outside an approved program`
        `in a period of ineligibility under SAR 2014 s 18 or SAID s 20` IS `is serving a period of ineligibility under other assistance regulations`)

§ `How much of our income counts`

@export How much of my household's earned income is exempt each month under SIS Regulations s 2-7(2)(a)?
GIVEN `I have a spouse in the household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse or partner (including someone you have lived with for 3 months and share finances with) is part of your household
      `I have a dependent child in the household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a dependent child of you or your spouse is part of your household
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much earned income is exempt` MEANS
    `the s 2-7(2)(a) earned income exemption` `I have a spouse in the household` `I have a dependent child in the household`

@export How much of my household's monthly income counts against Saskatchewan Income Support under SIS Regulations s 2-7?
GIVEN `I have a spouse in the household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse or partner is part of your household
      `I have a dependent child in the household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a dependent child of you or your spouse is part of your household
      `our gross pay from jobs` IS A NUMBER @desc Gross employment earnings of you and your spouse in the month (not your children's), in dollars
      `income tax, CPP and EI taken off our pay` IS A NUMBER @desc Income tax, Canada Pension Plan and Employment Insurance deducted from that pay, in dollars
      `other deductions our employer requires` IS A NUMBER @desc Other deductions your employer requires as a condition of employment (for example union dues), in dollars
      `our net self-employment income` IS A NUMBER @desc Self-employment income after the reasonable expenses the ministry allows, in dollars; 0 if none
      `child support we receive` IS A NUMBER @desc Child support received in the month, in dollars
      `of it, for special or extraordinary expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc Of that child support, the part an order or agreement sets for special or extraordinary expenses over the Federal Child Support Guidelines table amount, in dollars; 0 if none
      `gifts, prizes and winnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Gifts, prizes, winnings and incidental money received by the household in the month, in dollars
      `money from exempt sources` IS A NUMBER @desc Money that is fully exempt: Canada Child Benefit, Canada Child Disability Benefit, GST/HST credit, income tax refunds, Canada Workers Benefit, Canada Disability Benefit, RDSP money, foster care payments and the other sources listed in s 2-7(2), in dollars
      `all our other income` IS A NUMBER @desc All other money you and your spouse received or were eligible to receive in the month (for example EI, CPP, Old Age Security, WCB, pensions, rental income), in dollars
      `overpayments recovered from us by set-off` IS A NUMBER @desc Any overpayment recovered from you by set-off in the month, in dollars; 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of our income counts` MEANS
    `the household's income under s 2-7`
        (`Monthly moneys` WITH
            `gross earnings from employment`   IS `our gross pay from jobs`
            `income tax, CPP and EI deducted`  IS `income tax, CPP and EI taken off our pay`
            `deductions the employer requires` IS `other deductions our employer requires`
            `net self-employment income`       IS `our net self-employment income`
            `child support received`           IS `child support we receive`
            `special or extraordinary expenses portion of child support` IS `of it, for special or extraordinary expenses`
            `gifts, prizes, winnings and incidental moneys` IS `gifts, prizes and winnings`
            `moneys from fully exempt sources` IS `money from exempt sources`
            `all other moneys`                 IS `all our other income`
            `overpayments recovered by set-off` IS `overpayments recovered from us by set-off`)
        `I have a spouse in the household` `I have a dependent child in the household`

§ `Do our assets keep us out`

@export Are my household's liquid assets over the Saskatchewan Income Support limit of $2,000 per household member (SIS Regulations s 2-6(4))?
GIVEN `our cash, bank accounts, investments, RRSPs and other liquid assets` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of cash, bank deposits, money owed to you on demand, and the realizable value of stocks, bonds, unlocked pensions, RRSPs, RRIFs, trust interests, bequests, settlements and damages awards, for you and your spouse, not counting exempt items such as an RDSP or RESP, in dollars
      `cash surrender value of our life insurance` IS A NUMBER @desc The cash surrender value of your life insurance policies, in dollars (only the part over $1,500 counts)
      `number of people in my household` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are in your household: you, your spouse, and your dependent children
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are our liquid assets over the limit` IF
    `the liquid assets exceed the s 2-6(4) limit` (`the household's liquid assets` `our cash, bank accounts, investments, RRSPs and other liquid assets` `cash surrender value of our life insurance`) `number of people in my household`

@export Does my household own excess assets that rule out Saskatchewan Income Support, under SIS Regulations ss 1-2 and 2-6(5)(a)?
GIVEN `we own real property other than our home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or your spouse own land or buildings other than your principal residence
      `our equity in secondary or recreational vehicles` IS A NUMBER @desc Your total equity in vehicles that are not your main way of getting around, and recreational vehicles (boats, RVs, snowmobiles), in dollars
      `the ministry decided not to count the asset` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the ministry has decided not to treat the asset as an excess asset (for example for genuine social or economic reasons, s 2-10)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do we own excess assets` IF
    `owns excess assets` `we own real property other than our home` `our equity in secondary or recreational vehicles` `the ministry decided not to count the asset`

§ `Are we eligible, and how much`

@export Does my household have a budget deficit under SIS Regulations s 2-6?
GIVEN `our counted monthly income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your household's monthly income that counts under s 2-7 (see the income question), in dollars
      `our total monthly benefits on the ministry's schedule` IS A NUMBER @desc The total monthly benefits your household would get under the ministry's schedule of rates (adult basic, shelter and other benefits), in dollars; the regulations leave these amounts to the minister
      `our liquid assets are over the limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your liquid assets are over $2,000 per household member (see that question)
      `we own excess assets` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you own excess assets (see that question)
      `the ministry found we disposed of assets to qualify` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the ministry is satisfied that in the 6 months before you applied someone in the household gave away assets or made an unusual expenditure to qualify
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do we have a budget deficit` IF
    `has a budget deficit under s 2-6` `our counted monthly income` `our total monthly benefits on the ministry's schedule` `our liquid assets are over the limit` `we own excess assets` `the ministry found we disposed of assets to qualify`

@export Is my household eligible for Saskatchewan Income Support under SIS Regulations s 2-4?
GIVEN `I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have submitted an application
      `we have a budget deficit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your household has a budget deficit (see that question)
      `our resources do not cover a basic need` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your household's money and assets are not enough for one or more needs SIS covers (food, clothing, shelter, utilities and the other Part 4 needs)
      `we gave the consents asked for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your spouse have given the consents the ministry asked for to confirm eligibility
      `we applied for every other benefit we may get` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your spouse have explored every way to meet your needs, including applying for other government benefits you may be eligible for (such as EI, CPP or Old Age Security), even early
      `other assistance we receive` IS AN `Other assistance received` @desc Other assistance you or your spouse receive: none, Saskatchewan Assistance Regulations, 2014 benefits, SAID benefits, SAID temporary benefits under SAID s 17, federal resettlement assistance, or other similar benefits
      `we take part in case planning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your spouse take part in case planning with the ministry
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are we eligible` IF
    `the household is eligible under s 2-4` `I have applied` `we have a budget deficit` `our resources do not cover a basic need` `we gave the consents asked for` `we applied for every other benefit we may get` `other assistance we receive` `we take part in case planning`

@export How much Saskatchewan Income Support will my household be paid for a month, under SIS Regulations s 3-1?
GIVEN `our total monthly benefits on the ministry's schedule` IS A NUMBER @desc The total monthly benefits your household is eligible for under the ministry's schedule of rates, in dollars
      `our counted income last month` IS A NUMBER @desc Your household's income that counts under s 2-7, received in the previous month, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much will we be paid` MEANS
    `the monthly benefit under s 3-1` `our total monthly benefits on the ministry's schedule` `our counted income last month`

@export For how many months after a lump sum is my household not eligible for Saskatchewan Income Support, under SIS Regulations s 3-3(1)?
GIVEN `the lump sum` IS A NUMBER @desc The lump sum payment you or your spouse received (for example a settlement, an inheritance or retroactive benefits), in dollars
      `our total monthly benefits on the ministry's schedule` IS A NUMBER @desc The total monthly benefits your household would otherwise receive, in dollars
      `our counted monthly income without the lump sum` IS A NUMBER @desc Your household's monthly income that counts under s 2-7, not counting the lump sum, in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`For how many months are we self-supporting` MEANS
    `the s 3-3(1) months of self-support` `the lump sum` `our total monthly benefits on the ministry's schedule` `our counted monthly income without the lump sum`

§ `Deadlines for appeals -- if I disagree with a decision`

@export By what date must I appeal a Saskatchewan Income Support decision to the ministry, under SIS Regulations s 3-12(1)?
GIVEN `the date of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The date of the decision you disagree with
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I appeal to the ministry` MEANS `the last day to appeal under s 3-12(1)` `the date of the decision`

@export By what date must I give notice of appeal to the appeal board, under SIS Regulations s 3-14(2)?
GIVEN `the date the appeal committee's written decision was given` IS A DATE @desc The date the appeal committee gave its decision in writing
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I appeal to the appeal board` MEANS
    `the last day to appeal to the appeal board under s 3-14(2)` `the date the appeal committee's written decision was given`

§ `Overpayments -- if the ministry says I was overpaid`

@export By what date must I apply to the Court of King's Bench to review an overpayment certificate, under The Saskatchewan Assistance Act s 29.6(1)?
GIVEN `the date the notice was mailed or handed to me` IS A DATE @desc The date the notice of the filed certificate was handed to you, or mailed to you by registered mail
      `it came by registered mail` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice was sent by registered mail (it is then treated as served on the seventh day after mailing)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I apply for review of a certificate` MEANS
    `the last day to apply for review of an overpayment certificate` `the date the notice was mailed or handed to me` `it came by registered mail`

@export What is the earliest date the ministry may file an overpayment certificate against me in court, under The Saskatchewan Assistance Act s 29.5(2)?
GIVEN `the date of the notice of my right to appeal, or of the appeal decision` IS A DATE @desc The date you were given written notice of your right to appeal the overpayment (if you did not appeal), or the date your appeal was decided
GIVETH A DATE
`When may a certificate be filed against me` MEANS
    `the earliest day a certificate may be filed` `the date of the notice of my right to appeal, or of the appeal decision`

@export Can my Saskatchewan Income Support payments be garnished, seized or assigned, under The Saskatchewan Assistance Act s 29.7?
GIVEN `it is the ministry recovering an overpayment from future payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the deduction is the ministry recovering an overpayment from your future benefit payments (rather than a creditor's garnishment, seizure or assignment)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my payments be taken` IF
    `a payment may be taken from me` `it is the ministry recovering an overpayment from future payments`

§ `Offences -- if I am charged`

@export What is the most I can be fined, and imprisoned in default of payment, for an offence under The Saskatchewan Assistance Act ss 27 and 28?
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence` @desc The offence: contravening the Act, a regulation or an order (s 27); knowingly giving false information or concealing information to obtain assistance (s 28(1)); or continuing to receive assistance after receiving assets, knowing I am no longer eligible (s 28(3))
GIVETH A `Penalty`
`What is the most I can be fined` MEANS `the maximum penalty for an individual` `the offence`
